# Negative-control mutant — resolveExcludeDelegated's remembered-preference
# arm (pure derivation, NOT an AC-18 seam proof)
#
# What this mutant proves: `contract-product.utils.test.ts`'s pure-function
#   coverage of `resolveExcludeDelegated`'s three-argument derivation. It does
#   NOT prove `contract-product.feature`'s AC-18 scenario ("My choice about
#   delegated products is remembered") — that scenario promises the client's
#   choice is PERSISTED and RE-READ across sessions via the
#   `client-personal-details` seam, which this pure function never touches
#   (its `preference` argument is a plain boolean handed in by the caller).
#   AC-18 is a registered, unproven gap
#   (`contract-product.traceability.test.ts`'s `SCENARIO_GAPS`, and the
#   disclaimer docblock that opens
#   `contract-product.utils.test.ts`'s
#   `describe("resolveExcludeDelegated — the exclude_delegated flag the scope
#   sends")`) — no line number is cited here on purpose: the two earlier
#   revisions of this header both cited one, and both were orphaned by a later
#   insertion above the block. The describe title is the anchor, and
#   `contract-product.traceability.test.ts`'s
#   "the AC-18 disclaimer this patch header cites still opens
#   resolveExcludeDelegated's describe" check fails if it moves or is reworded.
#   No capture for the seam exists on disk and recording is forbidden this pass.
#   This patch grades the derivation alone, so it is renamed off the
#   AC-18-shaped filename that implied otherwise.
#
# AC-18's OWN @negative-control mutant — WITHHELD, and why (review W1).
#   AC-18's last line, "recording only the choice that changed, rather than the
#   whole set of preferences my account already holds, turns this scenario red",
#   names a WRITE. The seam it names is one line, and it is in neither module
#   this story owns:
#     packages/headless/src/modules/client-personal-details/client-personal-details.services.ts
#     `update()` — `diff.meta = { ...record.value.meta, ...diff.meta };`
#   That merge IS the "whole set of preferences" the criterion protects: the PUT
#   replaces the `meta` bag wholesale, so deleting the merge records only the
#   changed key. That deletion is the mutant AC-18 asks for.
#
#   It is not authored, for two causes, either sufficient on its own:
#     1. SCOPE. Ruling R21 scopes this run to `modules/contract/` and
#        `modules/contract-product/`. `client-personal-details` is a third
#        module. `contract-product` only READS the preference
#        (`createShowDelegatedPreference` -> `filterFields([...])` -> the model)
#        and holds no write path at all; bdd.md:160-174 puts AC-18's write half
#        in that third module's own two scenarios, under task T10d.
#     2. DEAD CONTROL. A mutant is a control only if a NAMED test flips. No test
#        in either module drives the write, and no test in
#        `client-personal-details/__tests__/` asserts the merged `meta` bag —
#        its nearest control, `client-personal-details.diff-only.must-fail.patch`,
#        grades `mapIProfileFields`'s diff, not the merge. A patch that flips
#        nothing would restage exactly the misrepresentation the prior
#        `delegated-preference` filename was pulled for.
#
#   What unblocks it: the `client-personal-details` preference-write capture
#   (bdd.md T10d). Recording is forbidden this pass, so the capture is a
#   REPORTED gap, not a silent one — AC-18 stays in `SCENARIO_GAPS`, so the
#   traceability gate names it on every run until the mutant lands.
# Test that goes red: contract-product.utils.test.ts >
#   "the client's own excludeDelegatedProducts preference, set false, forces
#   exclude_delegated=0 outside the delegated view"
#   (`resolveExcludeDelegated(undefined, false, true)` returns `1`, not `0`,
#   so `expect(...).toBe(0)` flips).
# Mutation: `resolveExcludeDelegated` drops the `preference === false` arm, so
#   an explicit "show delegated" preference falls through to the
#   no-preference default and is forgotten.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
index 34fab8669..d3dcc2a75 100644
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
@@ -110,7 +110,6 @@ export function resolveExcludeDelegated(
 ): 0 | 1 {
   if (scopeContext?.type === ContractProductsContextTypes.DELEGATED) return 0;
   if (preference === true) return 1;
-  if (preference === false) return 0;
   return hasDelegatedProducts ? 1 : 0;
 }

